y: observability.sh:351-354 publishes gate_scratch_mounted as 1/0; alarm at monitoring_autodeploy.tf:423-424 uses threshold=1, LessThanThreshold — a two-value space that cannot represent three classifications."],"finding":"AC6/§5 requires emitting a metric from assert_volumes_in_service.py's three-value classification (IN_SERVICE / NOT-IN-SERVICE / UNKNOWN) into the observability path, but never defines the emitted metric's value vocabulary nor how the three enum members map onto it — leaving the distinctness the script deliberately preserves (UNKNOWN != NOT-IN-SERVICE) at risk of being silently collapsed by a binary heartbeat.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f461fb3cd6a6a007f","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"AC6 / §5 'Land the declared-vs-provisioned check'","norm_id":"n917fff08b5efe885","priority":0.8,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor maps NOT-IN-SERVICE and UNKNOWN both to metric value 0, re-introducing the exact conflation the source script was written to prevent.","Executor emits a new metric but the alarm/threshold semantics for the UNKNOWN value are left undefined, so a 'could not determine' state pages (or fails to page) unpredictably."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"module","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiab