s cannot diverge silently'","Plan states classifications 'in-service / NOT-IN-SERVICE / UNKNOWN' but Verification only says 'must pass local verification' with no named divergence/failure-path test","ABSENCE: no test scenario exercising the NOT-IN-SERVICE path or asserting the correct metric value is emitted when live mount and declaration diverge"],"finding":"AC6 extends assert_volumes_in_service.py with new gate-scratch classification logic and a metric-emission path, but the plan specifies no test that the check actually DETECTS the divergence it exists to catch — i.e. that it classifies gate-scratch as NOT-IN-SERVICE and emits the failing metric when the live mount diverges from the Terraform declaration/state (the S1 mode). 'Local verification' plus Gerrit +1s does not name a failure-path/divergence test, so the check could land green while never firing on the very condition it targets.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f674adf6da21ddd7a","impact":0.67,"is_primary":null,"location":"AC6 / Verification: 'The declared-vs-provisioned check is a code change that must pass local verification...'","norm_id":"n37483c953f89a716","priority":0.3723,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Specify in Verification a unit/integration test that feeds synthetic lsblk output where the gate-scratch volume is declared in the Terraform join but absent/unmounted in live output, and assert the classifier returns NOT-IN-SERVICE and the emission path publishes the non-healthy metric value.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.5556,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","pat